{"ts":"2026-07-25T12:26:56.829Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gw6uyq"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Fleet attribution analytics: per-harness and per-model throughput, rework, and defect-escape rates derived from immutable history alone"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Once identity carries harness and model, the immutable history streams already contain everything needed to answer the questions a fleet operator actually has, with no new stored state and no telemetry: which model's work is reopened most often; which harness produces the most unresolved-validation warnings; how completion time distributes per model on comparable item types; which model's closes later attract a defect item linked by discovered_from; how much of a workspace's mutation volume is annotation versus state change per agent class. These are derivations over the same append-only streams that pm-pee5 uses for flow metrics, restricted and grouped by the provenance dimensions rather than by item. The output must be bounded and comparable: rates and distributions with sample counts, never raw per-entry dumps, and never a leaderboard that invites optimizing the metric. Explicitly out of scope: using these numbers as an authorization or routing input — detected identity is an unverified claim, and pm-3oqjnc owns allocation decisions on capability declarations, not on inferred quality scores."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["analytics","area:sdk","identity","observability","provenance","scale"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-25T12:26:56.829Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-25T12:26:56.829Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":420},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Analytics are pure derivations over immutable history with no new stored state and no telemetry dependency; Grouping is available by harness, by model, and by author_source, and every reported figure carries its sample count and window; A metric with an insufficient sample is reported as insufficient rather than as a number, so small workspaces get honest output; Output is bounded by the same token-budget contract as other read surfaces and degrades deterministically instead of dumping entries; The documentation states that these figures are observational, that detected identity is unverified, and that the figures must not be used as an authorization or allocation input; A workspace with no model provenance (pre-capture history) produces correct harness-level output and reports the model dimension as unavailable rather than empty"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"A fleet operator can compare agent classes on evidence already recorded, without instrumenting anything"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Thousands of concurrent agents of different models are the target deployment; without per-model attribution there is no way to tell an improving fleet from a degrading one"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Adds derived read-only analytics over existing streams; introduces a real risk of metric-gaming that the acceptance criteria must bound"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"Model and harness selection for a workspace becomes an evidence-backed decision instead of a preference"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5oj5"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":65},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-03pq3o","kind":"blocked_by","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:26:56.829Z"},{"id":"pm-3oqjnc","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:26:56.829Z"},{"id":"pm-5oj5","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:26:56.829Z"},{"id":"pm-pee5","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:26:56.829Z"},{"id":"pm-qwuber","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:26:56.829Z"},{"id":"pm-u14c","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:26:56.829Z"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"44d08c4eb3890d45f908227f85ef48a7cf71cec9b9df226c027b256372c63eb7","message":"File fleet attribution analytics as the consumer that makes model provenance actionable"}
